  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Implemented a reusable exact coefficient prefix and prepared analytic evaluation cache in lseries.py, plus exact topology reuse, packed source-transparent binary64 edge quadrature, branch/sign preselection, reusable conjugation action, and sealed result caches in periods.py. Added focused differential/evidence/cache tests and a resident Sage.js/PARI benchmark harness. Binary64 period work is explicitly capped at 44 evidence bits; higher requested precision requires two arbitrary-precision refinements before it is advertised.",
    "risks": [
      "Public periods above 44 bits still spend most of their time in two mpmath quadrature refinements and remain orders of magnitude slower than PARI's hyperellperiods.",
      "The packed coefficient fast path requires the coordinated hyp-local-stream-perf API to be integrated before this commit; otherwise lseries.py deliberately uses its exact legacy fallback.",
      "The production native-kernel registry entry and Float64Buffer WebAssembly bridge are shared integration/native-compiler work outside this lane's claims.",
      "The new analytic performance test needs an integration-lane test-manifest entry; pnpm test:changed otherwise fails only the manifest coverage check."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Integrate hyp-local-stream-perf before this implementation so GlobalCoefficientPrefix consumes rational_local_coefficient_chunks.",
      "Register hyperelliptic-period-edge-batch-production in architecture/native-kernels.json and land the coordinated Float64Buffer WebAssembly bridge.",
      "Replace the remaining two arbitrary-precision per-node mpmath quadratures with a batched Arb/Acb or equivalently source-transparent high-precision kernel while retaining the outer refinement and Riemann gates.",
      "Add test/hyperelliptic-analytic-performance.cjs to the shared test manifest, preferably in a slow/non-routine tier."
    ]
  }
